//@version=6
// ============================================================================
//  FLASHGOLD DIRECTION FILTER  -  v1.3 (buy zone / sell zone / no trade)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  v1.3 = v1.2 plus the optional SCORE VETO (group "Score veto", off by
//  default), with adjustable cut-offs and an accuracy-vs-coverage table,
//  and the information-only REVERSE-OLD-SIGNAL READOUT (off by default).
//  With the veto off it trades exactly like v1.2.
//
//  The entry signal of "FlashGold v5 Strategy (XAUUSD)" used as a direction
//  PERMISSION for your other strategies. It never opens, closes or manages a
//  trade: the strategy's entry stop order, stop loss, take profit, trailing
//  stop, time stop and sizing are all gone. It only answers, on every bar:
//  "is a BUY allowed now? is a SELL allowed now?". Your strategy keeps its
//  own entries and exits; an entry the filter does not allow is not taken.
//
//  THE RULE
//    Each FlashGold signal (BUY or SELL) sets the LEVEL = the signal price.
//      BUYS  are allowed only while price is ABOVE the level (BUY ZONE).
//      SELLS are allowed only while price is BELOW the level (SELL ZONE).
//      Around the level (the no-trade band) nothing is allowed (NO TRADE).
//    One level for both sides, whichever signal set it. The next signal
//    (buy or sell) replaces it. Before the first signal nothing is allowed.
//    Example: SELL signal at 2650.00, ATR(14) 10, band 0.25 ATR = 2.50 ->
//             sells pass while price < 2647.50, buys while price > 2652.50,
//             nothing in between, until the next signal. With the band at 0
//             the level alone splits them (the original rule).
//    "Level" = Entry price (default): the FlashGold entry price of the
//    signal, where the strategy put its stop order: ask + entry distance for
//    a BUY, bid - entry distance for a SELL. Right after a BUY signal price
//    is still below that level, so buys wait for the break above it (and the
//    band) and sells are allowed below the band (the mirror after a SELL).
//    "Signal close"
//    uses the close of the signal candle instead.
//
//  ZONES  (what you may do now)
//    Each signal's level splits the chart into zones, named in the status
//    box and, while the permission is in force, shaded (green, red, gray)
//    with the zone names at the last candle:
//      BUY ZONE    price above the level (+ the band): buys allowed, sells not.
//      SELL ZONE   price below the level (- the band): sells allowed, buys not.
//      NO TRADE    price inside the band around the level (it has not chosen
//                  a side yet), or against the signal with that switched
//                  off, or the side switched off, or, with the score veto
//                  on, the score disagreeing: nothing allowed (gray).
//                  Before the first signal and after a Minutes / Candles
//                  permission ends nothing is allowed either (no shade).
//    The band's edges are rounded outward to the tick grid, so the price
//    shown is the price that is still NO TRADE: BUY ZONE starts one tick
//    above it, SELL ZONE one tick below the lower edge.
//    "No-trade band": +- this many ATR(14) of the filter timeframe, taken at
//    the signal candle (0 = no band, the level alone).
//    SIGNAL DIRECTION: a BUY signal is CONFIRMED while price is above the
//    band (level + band) - buy, if Allow buys is on; while price is in the
//    band or below, it is NOT
//    confirmed - do not buy (the mirror for a SELL; with that side switched
//    off the box says so). Below a BUY signal's
//    level the SELL ZONE still allows sells, against the signal; turn
//    "Allow trading against the signal" off to make that side NO TRADE too:
//    then only the signal's own direction is ever allowed, and only once
//    price has confirmed it.
//
//  DIRECTION SCORE  (group "Direction score", off by default; information
//  only, the zones never use it)
//    Three ways to read a direction from the signals: Level side = UP above
//    the level, DOWN below it (the zones with no band, trading against the
//    signal allowed); Signal direction = the last signal's side, held until
//    the next signal; Signal reversed = the opposite side.
//    How often each one's direction was right, measured live on the filter
//    timeframe's own candles: UP is right when the close 1 (and H) filter
//    candles later is higher, DOWN when it is lower. Buys and sells are
//    averaged, so a market that just drifts up does not count as accuracy:
//    50% = a coin flip. Over the last N filter candles (or all history). It
//    scores "until next signal" (Minutes / Candles
//    windows are not scored).
//    BTC/USD 2023-01 .. 2026-10 (Bitstamp 1-minute data; Level = Entry
//    price, parent = the filter timeframe, child zones 1-3 at 1, 2 and 4 x
//    the filter timeframe (8H: 8H / 16H / 1D) with at least 2 aligned, the
//    other signal inputs at their defaults - the input defaults match this
//    only on 1H), tested out of sample on 2025-07 .. 2026-10, next candle /
//    10 candles later:
//      1m   level side 50% / 50%,  signal direction 50% / 49%,  reversed 50% / 51%
//      5m   level side 51% / 51%,  signal direction 49% / 49%,  reversed 51% / 51%
//      15m  level side 51% / 51%,  signal direction 48% / 48%,  reversed 52% / 52%
//      30m  level side 51% / 52%,  signal direction 49% / 48%,  reversed 51% / 52%
//      1H   level side 50% / 49%,  signal direction 48% / 50%,  reversed 52% / 50%
//      2H   level side 49% / 52%,  signal direction 49% / 48%,  reversed 51% / 52%
//      4H   level side 49% / 53%,  signal direction 49% / 48%,  reversed 51% / 52%
//      8H   level side 51% / 48%,  signal direction 48% / 51%,  reversed 52% / 49%
//      1D   level side 49% / 57%,  signal direction 53% / 43%,  reversed 47% / 57%
//    On BTC the signal's own direction, averaged over 1, 3 and 10 candles,
//    is right a little LESS than half the time on every tested timeframe
//    from 1m to 1D, in and out of sample (47-50%; 1m 49.5% / 49.6%): the
//    burst that makes a FlashGold signal more often ends a short move than
//    starts one, so its reverse scores a little more than half. Used as a
//    held direction, the TDI parent and the Fractal Direction Framework
//    trend average 48-49% too, the zone permission 47-48%. Quality
//    conditions on the signal (TDI lines, volatility, Hurst, the framework)
//    whose signals were right 53-58% of the time 20 candles later in sample
//    (61-68% on 4H and 8H, on 60-110 signals) scored 42-50% out of sample
//    (4H: 54%, on about 50 signals); held as a direction until the next
//    signal (tested on 15m, 30m, 1H and 1D) they were right only 50-52% in
//    sample and 46-50% out of sample. The best out-of-sample scores, 52-55%,
//    came on 2H-1D; of those, only "Signal reversed" with the parent at
//    2 x or 8 x the filter timeframe on 2H (4H, 16H), at 1D on 4H and at 3D
//    on 8H, and "Level side" with the parent at 2 x on 4H were also above
//    51% in sample (51.1-52.2%). Those runs read the parent's last closed
//    candle; this filter reads a parent above the filter timeframe from its
//    forming candle live (keep the parent = the filter timeframe). Check the
//    score on your own symbol and timeframe before relying on any rule.
//
//  SCORE VETO  (group "Score veto", OFF by default: with the switch off
//  nothing in this section changes a permission; it only adds two
//  request.security calls, Data Window rows and the input group)
//    A frozen logistic score, read from the filter's own state at the close
//    of each filter candle, says UP, DOWN or undecided. With the veto on, a
//    BUY ZONE allows buys only while the score says UP and a SELL ZONE
//    allows sells only while it says DOWN; the veto never allows what the
//    zones forbid, it only removes. Its 17 inputs: the zone, the distance
//    from the level in ATR of the signal candle, the last signal's side, the
//    1 / 5 / 20-candle returns in ATR, ATR over its 100-candle average, the
//    signal's age, zone x volatility, distance x volatility, the Fractal
//    Direction Framework structure direction (pivots 5 / 3) and the TDI fast
//    line's level and slope on the filter timeframe (this candle) and on 2 x
//    and 4 x it (their last bar closed by this candle's open). One model per
//    filter timeframe: 5m, 15m, 30m, 1H, fitted on BTC/USD 2020-01 .. 2025-12
//    (Bitstamp 1-minute data) and frozen before any 2026 test; on any other
//    timeframe the veto is NOT applied (the status box says so, the zones
//    decide alone). Until its inputs exist (100 filter candles, the 4 x
//    child's RSI) nothing is allowed. Coefficients, definitions and tests:
//    calibration/wf/VETO_PORT_CONTRACT.md, results/veto/.
//    What it did, zone alone -> zone + veto, raw accuracy of the allowed side
//    at the next filter candle (and the share of candles with a permission):
//      these coefficients, fresh broker BTCUSD 2026-07 .. 2026-10, 5m: 51.0%
//        -> 52.1% (95% CI of the gain +0.6 .. +1.5 points), permission on
//        84% -> 53% of candles; these coefficients on Bitstamp 2026-01 .. 10
//        UTC bars (a window looked at during the design; no CI): +1.4 / +1.9
//        / +1.2 / +2.2 points on 5m / 15m / 30m / 1H;
//      the same recipe refitted walk-forward per half-year (not these
//        coefficients), Bitstamp 2018-2019, never looked at before the test:
//        5m 51.5% -> 56.1%, 15m 51.4% -> 55.6%, 30m 50.9% -> 55.1%, 1H 50.8%
//        -> 56.4%, of which, on 5m, about 1-2 points are that era's
//        last-trade bounce (about 0.2 on 30m; 15m and 1H not measured);
//        2021-2022 (looked at during the design): +1.9 / +2.4 / +1.8
//        / +3.0; permission on 84% -> 40-54% of candles in every window.
//    The gain is small, varies by era and removes a third to a half of the
//    permissions; 1H was reported, not part of the rule. In "Tick" mode the
//    zone is the live one while the score is the last closed filter
//    candle's (the research judged both at the candle's close: "Candle
//    close" on the filter's own timeframe). The model was calibrated with the
//    signal inputs at the v1.2 defaults, the band at 0.25, Level = Entry
//    price, parent = the filter timeframe and the child zones at 1 / 2 / 4 x
//    it (at least 2 aligned): the status box lists any setting that differs.
//    The 30m and 1H models read 2H / 4H bars that, in the calibration, began
//    on the broker's clock (UTC+2 / +3); TradingView's begin at 00:00 UTC,
//    so those two models see shifted bars (5m and 15m are unaffected). The
//    zone's tick rounding uses the symbol's tick (0.01 in the calibration).
//    Compare the Data Window inputs ("Score inputs in the Data Window") with
//    calibration/wf/results/veto/pine_parity/ on BITSTAMP:BTCUSD; on the
//    live bar they show the forming filter candle.
//
//  VETO CUT-OFFS AND ACCURACY VS COVERAGE
//    The score says UP above its upper cut-off, DOWN below its lower one and
//    undecided in between. "Cut-offs" moves both away from (+) or toward (-)
//    the middle by that many times the model's own gap (upper - lower):
//      0     the model's cut-offs (the calibrated rule, default)
//      -0.5  both meet in the middle: every score is UP or DOWN, so the veto
//            blocks least (most permissions)
//      +1    a gap three times as wide: only strong scores decide, so the
//            veto blocks most (fewest permissions)
//    Wider cut-offs give fewer permissions; whether they are also right more
//    often is what the table measures. "Show accuracy vs coverage" adds it
//    to the status box, live on the filter timeframe's own candles, over the
//    direction-score window ("Window, filter candles"), for: the zones alone,
//    and the zones + veto at cut-offs -0.5, 0, +0.5, +1, +2 (and yours, if
//    different). For each: ACCURACY = how often the allowed side was right
//    at the next filter candle's close (buys and sells averaged, 50% = coin
//    flip; the zone judged at the candle's close, as the research did),
//    COVERAGE = the share of filter candles with a permission, and the number
//    of scored calls. It reads closed filter candles only (one candle
//    behind the forming one) and never changes a permission. Rows with fewer
//    than 100 calls are gray: too few to tell 52% from 50%. Pick a setting
//    on a window you did not use to choose it, and check it again later: the
//    model was fitted on BTC/USD 2020-2025, and choosing the best row on the
//    same history overstates it.
//
//  REVERSE-OLD-SIGNAL READOUT  (group "Reverse-old-signal readout", off by
//  default; information only: it never allows or blocks anything)
//    The rule under forward test: when the last FlashGold signal is 9 or more
//    filter candles old, call the OPPOSITE of its direction. Found on
//    TradingView 5m exports of BTCUSD, ETHUSD (2026-05..10) and OANDA XAUUSD
//    (2026-03..10): on a 15m filter it was right 53.5% (6 candles later) and
//    53.9% (12 candles later) over 843 signals pooled, above 50% in all three
//    markets; on 1H it pointed the other way (45-48%), so it is a lead, not
//    a result (docs/results/fgf_acc_cross_market.md). On ten earlier months
//    of BTC it had not been chosen on (15m export, 2025-08..2026-05) it
//    scored 50.7% / 50.0% over 477 signals: NOT CONFIRMED. It was picked after
//    looking, so only data after that counts: the readout scores calls made
//    on or after "Count accuracy from" (default 2026-10-18).
//    The status box shows the call now (and the age of the signal), and its
//    accuracy 6 and 12 filter candles later: buys and sells averaged (50% =
//    coin flip), number of calls and of distinct signals behind them (calls
//    under one signal overlap: the signals are the real sample). Set the
//    filter timeframe to 15 minutes to test the rule as found; on another
//    timeframe the box says so. Judge it after about 100+ signals: below
//    about 54% it is gone.
//
//  FILTER TIMEFRAME  (default 1 hour)
//    The signal runs on the candles of "Filter timeframe", every FlashGold
//    input working as on that timeframe's own chart. Put the filter on a 1m
//    chart, or paste it into a 1m strategy, with Filter timeframe = 1 hour:
//    it shows, and allows / blocks, what the 1H chart shows at that moment.
//      - A 1H signal counts when its 1H candle closes, at that candle's
//        level. Only closed 1H candles are read, so nothing repaints: the
//        signal mark sits on the first chart candle judged at or after that
//        close (Tick / Candle close: the candle that closes with it, or on a
//        higher chart the candle that contains it; Candle open: the first
//        candle that opens at or after it).
//      - Price is compared to the level at every chart candle: a 1m strategy
//        gets the 1H filter's answer at every 1m tick, open or close (see
//        CHECK PRICE ON).
//      - "Candles" counts 1H candles; "Minutes" runs on the clock.
//    "Chart" in the dropdown runs it on the chart's own candles. On a lower
//    chart the 1H history starts where the chart's history starts: the first
//    1H candles are a warm-up (RSI, ATR) and can differ from the 1H chart;
//    later candles match it.
//
//  INPUTS (group "Direction filter")
//    Enable filter      Off = buys and sells always allowed.
//    Filter timeframe   The timeframe the signal runs on (see above).
//    Level              Entry price (default) or Signal close (see above).
//    Permission lasts   Until next signal (default): the level stays in
//                       force until the next signal replaces it.
//                       Minutes / Candles: it also ends after that many
//                       minutes, or filter candles counted from the signal
//                       candle (1 = the signal candle only); then nothing is
//                       allowed until the next signal.
//    Check price on     When price is compared to the level (see below).
//    No-trade band      +- ATR mult around the level where nothing is
//                       allowed (see ZONES; 0 = off).
//    Allow trading against the signal  On: below a BUY level (- the band)
//                       sells are allowed (and above a SELL level (+ the
//                       band) buys). Off: only the
//                       signal's direction, once confirmed.
//    Allow buys/sells   Turn one side off completely.
//  Group "Direction score": show it, its window (filter candles, 0 = all
//  history) and its longer horizon H (filter candles).
//  Group "Score veto": the veto switch (off) and the Data Window inputs.
//  The "FlashGold signal" groups are the strategy's signal inputs, same
//  defaults, same logic: bid/ask model, TDI direction (fast line rising =
//  BUY), parent + six child zones, burst gate, prior drift, entry hold, one
//  signal per bar. ("TDI slow length" is left out: the direction never used
//  it.)
//
//  OUTPUTS (Data Window / "Source" dropdown of another script)
//    FGF buy allowed    1 when a buy may be taken on this bar, else 0.
//    FGF sell allowed   1 when a sell may be taken on this bar, else 0.
//    FGF active         1 while a signal's permission is in force.
//    FGF level          The level in force.
//    FGF signal         1 / -1 on the bar a BUY / SELL signal becomes known.
//    FGF ended          1 on the bar a Minutes / Candles permission ends.
//    FGF zone           1 BUY ZONE / -1 SELL ZONE / 0 NO TRADE, 2 when the
//                       filter is off (buys and sells allowed): what the
//                       buy / sell allowed outputs say, as one number.
//    FGF signal confirmed  1 while the permission is in force and price is
//                       past the band on the signal's side (price only: the
//                       Allow buys / sells switches are not applied; 0 when
//                       the filter is off or the permission has ended).
//    FGF score          The level rule's live direction score, next candle
//                       (0-1), when the score is on.
//    FGF score veto     With the veto on: 1 buys only, -1 sells only, 0
//                       nothing (score undecided or inputs not ready);
//                       2 when it is off, the filter is off, or no model
//                       exists for the filter timeframe (the zones decide
//                       alone).
//    FGF veto score     The score (log-odds; > 0 leans up) of the filter
//                       candle in force, when a model exists.
//    FGV in 1 .. 17, FGV score / answer (last filter candle)  The score's
//                       inputs, score and answer at the latest filter candle
//                       (closed bars: the latest filter candle closed by the
//                       bar's close; the live bar: the forming candle), with
//                       "Score inputs in the Data Window" on (parity check;
//                       the 2 x / 4 x rows only where a model exists).
//
//  HOW TO USE IT
//  A) Paste into your strategy (recommended)
//     Copy everything between BEGIN and END below into your strategy, under
//     its own inputs, and gate your entries:
//         if myBuySignal and fgfBuyOk
//             strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
//         if mySellSignal and fgfSellOk
//             strategy.entry("S", strategy.short)
//     Exits are never gated. Every name starts with "fgf", so nothing clashes
//     with your script (the FlashGold strategy included). If your script
//     runs in its own pane, set FGF_FORCE_OVERLAY = true. The block makes 16
//     request.security calls (a script may make 40) returning 63 tuple
//     values (a script's calls may return 127 together; the FlashGold v5
//     strategy's return 56, so both fit). To free 17, delete the "x1 ..
//     x17" / "fvX1 .. fvX17" tuple members and the "FGV in" plots.
//  B) Link without editing
//     Add this indicator to the chart. In your strategy add
//         fgfBuyExt  = input.source(close, "FG filter buy allowed")
//         fgfSellExt = input.source(close, "FG filter sell allowed")
//     pick the "FGF buy allowed" / "FGF sell allowed" plots in the strategy's
//     settings, and gate with   myBuySignal and fgfBuyExt == 1
//     (== 1: an unlinked source is still 'close' and must not count).
//
//  CHECK PRICE ON  (when price is compared to the level)
//    Tick (default)  The live price, on every tick: a buy is allowed the
//                    moment price trades past the BUY ZONE edge (level +
//                    band on the tick grid; the level itself with no band).
//                    Closed candles are
//                    judged at their close time with their close; this can
//                    differ from their last tick when a filter candle or a
//                    Minutes window ends with the candle. A Pine strategy
//                    acts on ticks only with calc_on_every_tick = true;
//                    otherwise it reads the close.
//    Candle open     Each candle's OPEN, at its open time. Decided on the
//                    candle's first tick and fixed for the whole candle.
//    Candle close    Each candle's CLOSE, at its close time. While a candle
//                    is forming it is judged at its open with the last
//                    closed candle's close: on a continuous chart that is the
//                    last closed candle's answer (after a gap or session
//                    break, signals and Minutes windows are judged at the
//                    new candle's open). The candle gets its own answer when
//                    it closes.
//    The signal in force is judged at the same moment: in Candle open, a 1H
//    signal counts from the first candle that opens at or after its 1H close.
//    Candle open and Candle close never change inside a candle.
//
//  TIMING
//  Every closed bar is judged at a fixed moment (its open or its close), on
//  history and live alike, so a strategy backtests as it runs live. While a
//  live bar is still forming, Tick uses the real clock (shading, status box,
//  gates). A Minutes permission covers the bars whose judging moment is in
//  [signal candle close, + minutes). With Tick + Minutes the status box and
//  the zone names at the last candle also end the permission by the real
//  clock (a closed market, delayed data); the shading, the lines, the gates
//  and the outputs keep the candle's own clock, so a last candle judged
//  inside the window stays shaded and its outputs keep their values while
//  the box says the permission ended. An order placed on the last allowed bar
//  fills on the next bar's open.
// ============================================================================
indicator("FlashGold Direction Filter", "FG-DF", overlay=true, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=500, max_bars_back=500)

// ===================== BEGIN FLASHGOLD DIRECTION FILTER ======================
// Set true when this block lives in a script that runs in its own pane
// (overlay=false) so the visuals are drawn on the price chart.
FGF_FORCE_OVERLAY = false

GRP_FGF = "Direction filter"
fgfOn        = input.bool(true, "Enable filter", group=GRP_FGF, tooltip="Off: buys and sells are always allowed. On: each FlashGold signal sets the level: BUY ZONE above it (+ the no-trade band), SELL ZONE below it (- the band), NO TRADE inside the band. Nothing is allowed before the first signal.")
fgfTf        = input.timeframe("60", "Filter timeframe", group=GRP_FGF, tooltip="The FlashGold signal runs on this timeframe's candles, and any chart (or strategy) using the filter gets the answer that timeframe's own chart shows at that moment: 1 hour on a 1m chart = the 1H view. Only closed candles are read, so nothing repaints. 'Chart' = this chart's own candles.")
fgfLvMode    = input.string("Entry price", "Level", options=["Entry price", "Signal close"], group=GRP_FGF, tooltip="Entry price: the FlashGold entry price of the signal (ask + entry distance for a BUY, bid - entry distance for a SELL). Signal close: the close of the signal candle.")
fgfLast      = input.string("Until next signal", "Permission lasts", options=["Until next signal", "Minutes", "Candles"], group=GRP_FGF, tooltip="Until next signal: the level stays in force until the next signal replaces it. Minutes / Candles: it also ends after that many minutes, or that many filter-timeframe candles counted from the signal candle (1 = the signal candle only); then nothing is allowed until the next signal.")
fgfMinutes   = input.int(60, "Minutes", minval=1, group=GRP_FGF)
fgfBars      = input.int(1, "Candles", minval=1, group=GRP_FGF)
fgfCheck     = input.string("Tick", "Check price on", options=["Tick", "Candle open", "Candle close"], group=GRP_FGF, tooltip="When price is compared to the level. Tick: the live price, on every tick (closed candles keep their close). Candle open: each candle's open, decided on its first tick and fixed for the whole candle. Candle close: each candle's close, decided when it closes; while a candle is forming it is judged at its open with the last closed candle's close.")
fgfBandAtr   = input.float(0.25, "No-trade band, ATR mult", minval=0.0, step=0.05, group=GRP_FGF, tooltip="NO TRADE zone around the level: +- this many ATR(14) of the filter timeframe at the signal candle. Inside it price has not chosen a side, so neither buys nor sells are allowed. 0 = no band: above the level BUY ZONE, below it SELL ZONE.")
fgfAgainst   = input.bool(true, "Allow trading against the signal", group=GRP_FGF, tooltip="On: below a BUY signal's level the SELL ZONE allows sells (and above a SELL signal's level the BUY ZONE allows buys). Off: those zones are NO TRADE; only the signal's own direction is allowed, and only once price confirms it.")
fgfAllowBuy  = input.bool(true, "Allow buys", inline="side", group=GRP_FGF)
fgfAllowSell = input.bool(true, "Allow sells", inline="side", group=GRP_FGF, tooltip="Turn one side off completely.")
fgfShowBg    = input.bool(true, "Shade", inline="vis", group=GRP_FGF)
fgfShowLv    = input.bool(true, "Level line", inline="vis", group=GRP_FGF)
fgfSigMark   = input.bool(true, "Signal marks", inline="vis", group=GRP_FGF, tooltip="Shade: green = BUY ZONE (buys allowed), red = SELL ZONE (sells allowed), gray = NO TRADE (inside the band, against the signal when that is off, that side turned off, or, with the score veto on, the score disagreeing). Level line: the signal's level, dashed lines: the band edges, names of the zones at the last candle. Signal marks: a triangle where a signal becomes known.")
fgfShowTbl   = input.bool(true, "Status box", inline="tbl", group=GRP_FGF)
fgfTblPos    = input.string("top_right", "", options=["top_right","middle_right","bottom_right","top_left","middle_left","bottom_left","top_center","bottom_center"], inline="tbl", group=GRP_FGF)

GRP_FGS = "Direction score"
fgsShow = input.bool(false, "Show the direction score", group=GRP_FGS, tooltip="In the status box: how often each of three readings of the signals (level side, signal direction, signal reversed) was right on the filter timeframe's candles, 1 and H candles later, buys and sells averaged (50% = a coin flip). Information only: the zones never use it.")
fgsWin  = input.int(500, "Window, filter candles (0 = all history)", minval=0, maxval=500, group=GRP_FGS)
fgsH    = input.int(10, "Longer horizon H, filter candles", minval=2, maxval=100, group=GRP_FGS)

GRP_FGV = "Score veto"
fgvOn  = input.bool(false, "Score veto: a zone allows its side only while the score agrees", group=GRP_FGV, tooltip="Off (default): the zones alone decide. On: a frozen logistic score, read from the filter's own state at the close of each filter candle, must also say UP for a buy (DOWN for a sell); it never allows what the zones forbid. Models exist for the 5m, 15m, 30m and 1H filter timeframes (BTC/USD, Bitstamp 2020-2025); on any other timeframe the veto is not applied and the status box says so. Until the score's inputs exist (about 100 filter candles of chart history) nothing is allowed. Out of sample it added about +1 to +2 points of next-candle accuracy and removed a third to a half of the permissions (see the header).")
fgvWiden = input.float(0.0, "Cut-offs: widen (+) / narrow (-), x the model's gap", minval=-0.5, maxval=5.0, step=0.25, group=GRP_FGV, tooltip="0 (default): the model's calibrated cut-offs. Above 0: the score must be further from the middle to say UP or DOWN, so the veto blocks more (fewer permissions). -0.5: both cut-offs meet in the middle and every score decides (fewest blocks). See 'Show accuracy vs coverage' for what each setting did on this chart.")
fgvCurveOn = input.bool(false, "Show accuracy vs coverage", group=GRP_FGV, tooltip="Status box: for the zones alone and for the zones + veto at several cut-offs, how often the allowed side was right at the next filter candle (buys and sells averaged, 50% = coin flip), the share of filter candles with a permission, and the number of scored calls, over the direction-score window. Information only: it never changes a permission. Models exist for 5m, 15m, 30m and 1H only.")
fgvDbg = input.bool(false, "Score inputs in the Data Window", group=GRP_FGV, tooltip="Adds the score's 17 inputs, its value and its answer at the latest filter candle (the forming one on the live bar) to the Data Window, to check them against the research export (calibration/wf/results/veto/pine_parity, BITSTAMP:BTCUSD).")

GRP_FGR = "Reverse-old-signal readout"
fgrShow = input.bool(false, "Show the reverse-old-signal readout", group=GRP_FGR, tooltip="Information only: never allows or blocks anything. When the last FlashGold signal is at least N filter candles old, the readout calls the opposite of its direction, and counts how often that call was right 6 and 12 filter candles later (buys and sells averaged, 50% = coin flip). Tested as found with Filter timeframe = 15 minutes. See the header.")
fgrAge  = input.int(9, "Signal at least this many filter candles old", minval=1, group=GRP_FGR, tooltip="9 in the test that found the rule. Change it and the forward test no longer tests the same rule.")
fgrFrom = input.time(timestamp("18 Oct 2026 00:00 +0000"), "Count accuracy from", group=GRP_FGR, tooltip="Only calls made on or after this time are scored. The rule was found on data up to 2026-10-17, so the default counts only data it was not chosen on.")

// ---- FlashGold signal inputs (the strategy's, same defaults) ----------------
GRP_FGC = "FlashGold signal: core"
fgfSpreadPts    = input.float(25.0, "Spread pts", minval=0.0, step=0.1, group=GRP_FGC, tooltip="Full spread in points (mintick units). Half of it offsets bid and ask.")
fgfEntryDistPts = input.float(50.0, "Entry distance pts (Points unit)", minval=0.0, step=0.1, group=GRP_FGC)
fgfHoldBars     = input.int(0, "Entry hold bars", minval=0, group=GRP_FGC)
fgfHoldFavPts   = input.float(5.0, "Hold min favorable pts (Points unit)", minval=0.0, step=0.1, group=GRP_FGC)
fgfOnePerBar    = input.bool(true, "One signal per bar", group=GRP_FGC)

GRP_FGB = "FlashGold signal: burst / direction"
fgfDistUnit     = input.string("ATR", "Burst / entry distance / hold unit", options=["ATR", "Points"], group=GRP_FGB, tooltip="ATR: the three thresholds below are multiples of ATR(14) of the filter timeframe. Points: the point inputs in the core group are used.")
fgfBurstAtr     = input.float(0.5, "Burst threshold, ATR mult (ATR unit)", minval=0.0, step=0.05, group=GRP_FGB)
fgfEntryDistAtr = input.float(0.25, "Entry distance, ATR mult (ATR unit)", minval=0.0, step=0.05, group=GRP_FGB)
fgfHoldFavAtr   = input.float(0.1, "Hold min favorable, ATR mult (ATR unit)", minval=0.0, step=0.05, group=GRP_FGB)
fgfBurstPts     = input.float(172.0, "Burst threshold pts (Points unit)", minval=0.0, step=0.1, group=GRP_FGB)
fgfUseBurst     = input.bool(true, "Require burst gate", group=GRP_FGB)
fgfAnyCombo     = input.bool(false, "Allow any combo", group=GRP_FGB, tooltip="If on, TDI parent/zone can approve direction even when burst is weaker.")
fgfDriftBars    = input.int(60, "Prior drift bars", minval=1, group=GRP_FGB)
fgfUseDrift     = input.bool(false, "Use prior drift filter", group=GRP_FGB)

GRP_FGZ = "FlashGold signal: TDI trade zone"
fgfUseZones   = input.bool(true, "Use TDI trade-zone filter", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfParentTf   = input.timeframe("60", "Parent obedience timeframe", group=GRP_FGZ, tooltip="Calibrated with the parent = the timeframe the signal runs on. Keep it equal to Filter timeframe: a parent above it reads its forming bar live, so it repaints.")
fgfRsiLen     = input.int(14, "TDI RSI length", minval=2, group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfFastLen    = input.int(2, "TDI white fast length", minval=1, group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfMinAligned = input.int(2, "Minimum child zones aligned", minval=0, maxval=6, group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfFlatParent = input.bool(false, "Allow trade if parent is flat", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfIgnoreNa   = input.bool(true, "Ignore zones without data", group=GRP_FGZ, tooltip="A child zone whose timeframe has no data on this candle is dropped from the active count instead of counting as MIX.")
fgfHtfClosed  = input.bool(true, "Higher-TF zones use the last CLOSED bar", group=GRP_FGZ, tooltip="A child zone on a timeframe HIGHER than the filter timeframe is read from its last closed bar, so history and live agree. Off: such a zone reads its forming bar live, so it repaints.")
fgfUseZ1 = input.bool(true, "Use child zone 1", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfZTf1  = input.timeframe("60", "Zone 1 timeframe", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfUseZ2 = input.bool(true, "Use child zone 2", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfZTf2  = input.timeframe("120", "Zone 2 timeframe", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfUseZ3 = input.bool(true, "Use child zone 3", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfZTf3  = input.timeframe("240", "Zone 3 timeframe", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfUseZ4 = input.bool(false, "Use child zone 4", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfZTf4  = input.timeframe("480", "Zone 4 timeframe", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfUseZ5 = input.bool(false, "Use child zone 5", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfZTf5  = input.timeframe("1", "Zone 5 timeframe", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfUseZ6 = input.bool(false, "Use child zone 6", group=GRP_FGZ)
fgfZTf6  = input.timeframe("2", "Zone 6 timeframe", group=GRP_FGZ)

// The timeframe the signal runs on ("Chart" = the chart's own).
string fgfTfEff = fgfTf == "" ? timeframe.period : fgfTf
int    fgfTfSec = timeframe.in_seconds(fgfTfEff)

// ---- Score veto: the frozen model of the filter timeframe ---------------------
